{
  "version": 1,
  "_comment": "ROCKE-owned architecture SSOT. Hardware facts only (no pipeline/scheduler vocabulary). MFMA atom sets are hardware-verified on real hardware (see dsl_docs/architecture/multi_arch_data_layout.md). Each MMA row: {family,a,b,c,m,n,k,op_id}; op_id is the opaque backend handle (matches IRBuilder.mfma_* today).",
  "_comment_async_lds_max_dwords": "Widest per-lane DRAM->LDS DMA the buffer_load_lds family can do, in dwords; 0 where the arch has no such instruction. This is NOT buffer_load_max_dwords: that one is the *register* vector buffer-load width (4 everywhere), while the load-*to-LDS* form is narrower. CDNA3 (gfx942) has only the dword form; the b96/b128 forms (dwords 3 and 4) arrived with CDNA4 (gfx950). Emitting a wider one than the arch supports does not produce a diagnostic -- the AMDGPU backend aborts the process with 'LLVM ERROR: Do not know how to expand this operator's operand!'.",
  "_comment_vmcnt_bits": "Width in bits of the vector-memory counter an s_waitcnt can wait on. On gfx9 the field is split across bits [3:0] and [15:14] of the immediate, so it is 6 bits wide, not 4. Measured with llvm-mc -show-encoding (LLVM 20, 22, 23 and 24): vmcnt(63) encodes and vmcnt(64) is refused on gfx90a, gfx942, gfx950, gfx1151 and gfx11-generic.",
  "generic_targets": {
    "_comment": "LLVM generic processors catalogued in arches, mapped to the concrete processors whose devices load their code objects (llvm.org/docs/AMDGPUUsage.html, generic processor table). Single source of membership for target.py; mirrored by rocke_ati_generic_targets in cpp/core/arch/data.cpp.",
    "gfx11-generic": ["gfx1100", "gfx1101", "gfx1102", "gfx1103", "gfx1150", "gfx1151", "gfx1152", "gfx1153", "gfx1154"],
    "gfx12-generic": ["gfx1200", "gfx1201"]
  },
